      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve \\(4^4 \\cdot 5^4\\), we can use the property of exponents which states that \\(a^m \\cdot b^m = (a \\cdot b)^m\\). Here, \\(a = 4\\), \\(b = 5\\), and \\(m = 4\\). So, we have:\n\n\\[\n4^4 \\cdot 5^4 = (4 \\cdot 5)^4 = 20^4\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate \\(20^4\\). We can do this by multiplying 20 by itself four times:\n\n\\[\n20^4 = 20 \\cdot 20 \\cdot 20 \\cdot 20\n\\]\n\nCalculating step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n20 \\cdot 20 = 400\n\\]\n\n\\[\n400 \\cdot 20 = 8000\n\\]\n\n\\[\n8000 \\cdot 20 = 160000\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(4^4 \\cdot 5^4\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{160000}\n\\]",
